WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience clapping)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- We can't talk about the Lakers

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:02.610
without mentioning Kobe Bryant.

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:03.720
He was here, I love him.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.530
I fell in love with them even in person.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.760
And that was one of those huge things,

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.410
and even if you didn't
know him personally,

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:10.410
it really did hit.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.440
I remember being in my house
and we finding it on the news.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.390
Like, it hit everyone.

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:16.660
And that's how powerful
I do think that sports

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.900
and those figures can
be for kids or adults,

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.280
and that excitement
and that place in time.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.145
And I don't know, and he
really supported you, I heard.

00:00:24.145 --> 00:00:27.230
So that must've been really
hard to come back from,

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.230
as a team.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:29.117
- Yeah.

00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:33.580
I mean, we all lost somebody
that was really special

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.440
and it's left a void in my life

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.320
and a void for all Laker fans.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:44.320
And I remember when my dad passed in 2013,

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.700
Kobe reached out to me

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.940
and invited me to have lunch
with him in Orange County.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:54.240
And he brought his daughter
Gianna along with him.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.890
And he said, "I hope you don't mind,

00:00:55.890 --> 00:01:00.300
I brought Gianna with me because
I wanted him to see a woman

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.780
in a position of power, and
hear what you had to say.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:05.613
- Yeah.

00:01:05.613 --> 00:01:08.540
And I know what he was doing
was really motivating me

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:13.100
because there's all these
little girls that are looking up

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.730
to a person like me in my position.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:18.886
And that's the kind of
thing that Kobe did,

00:01:18.886 --> 00:01:23.490
would motivate, he knew
how to motivate people

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:27.670
and to remind me of how
important what I'm doing is,

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:31.370
and through that we
can honor Kobe's memory

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:32.888
and that's how we keep his legacy alive.

00:01:32.888 --> 00:01:33.721
(audience clapping)

